      },
      "source": [
        "### 💼 Marketing Recommendations by Cluster\n",
        "\n",
        "Each cluster warrants a tailored CRM strategy aligned with CLTV maximisation [Gupta & Lehmann, 2005]:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **High Recency + High Frequency + High Monetary** → VIP retention: exclusive offers, loyalty rewards\n",
        "- **High Recency + Low Frequency** → Activation: welcome series, second-purchase incentive (10% off)\n",
        "- **Low Recency + High Frequency + High Monetary** → Win-back: personal outreach, \"We miss you\" campaign\n",
        "- **Low Recency + Low Frequency + Low Monetary** → Archive or minimal-cost reactivation email\n",
        "- **High Cancellation Rate** → Investigate root cause (product quality, delivery); proactive service\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "09a1ca42",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "09a1ca42"
      },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Section 9 — Recommendation System\n",
        "\n",
        "Architecture:\n",
        "1. **Popularity-based baseline** — top-N products per cluster\n",
        "2. **Item-to-item cosine similarity** using a sparse customer–product matrix [Linden et al., 2003]\n",
        "3. **Final output**: `recommendations_df` with CustomerID, Cluster, Rec1/2/3\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 47,
      "id": "5a2e1985",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "5a2e1985",
        "outputId": "7e017be1-eb25-40b7-9141-7e5b9e380474"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Top products per cluster (first 5 shown):\n",
            "  Cluster 0: [84946, '85099B', 22197, 15036, 23582]\n",
            "  Cluster 1: [84077, 84879, '85099B', 22197, '85123A']\n",
            "  Cluster 2: [84077, 22065, 84879, 22086, 21212]\n",
            "  Cluster 3: ['85123A', 16045, 22920, 84077, 84879]\n",
            "  Cluster 4: [84568]\n",
            "  Cluster 5: [22616, 62018, 22998, 17003, 21967]\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# ── 9.1  Cluster-level product popularity baseline ───────────────────────────\n",
        "# Attach cluster label to sales df\n",
        "cid_to_cluster = customer_clean['Cluster'].to_dict()\n",
        "df_rec = df_sales[df_sales['CustomerID'].isin(cid_to_cluster)].copy()\n",
        "df_rec['Cluster'] = df_rec['CustomerID'].map(cid_to_cluster)\n",
        "\n",
        "top_per_cluster = {}\n",
        "for cid in range(OPTIMAL_K):\n",
        "    sub = df_rec[df_rec['Cluster'] == cid]\n",
        "    top = (sub.groupby('StockCode')['Quantity'].sum()\n",
        "             .nlargest(50).index.tolist())\n",
        "    top_per_cluster[cid] = top\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Top products per cluster (first 5 shown):\")\n",
        "for cid, prods in top_per_cluster.items():\n",
        "    print(f\"  Cluster {cid}: {prods[:5]}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 48,
      "id": "08d550e3",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "08d550e3",
        "outputId": "e9482ae6-02c6-4d82-96f8-2a297728deb9"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Item similarity matrix: (3619, 3619)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# ── 9.2  Sparse customer–product matrix ─────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "# [Linden et al., 2003] item-to-item collaborative filtering\n",
        "purchase_matrix = (df_rec.groupby(['CustomerID','StockCode'])['Quantity']\n",
        "                   .sum().unstack(fill_value=0))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Cosine similarity between items\n",
        "item_sim = cosine_similarity(purchase_matrix.T.values)\n",
        "item_sim_df = pd.DataFrame(item_sim,\n",
        "                            index=purchase_matrix.columns,\n",
        "                            columns=purchase_matrix.columns)\n",
        "print(f\"Item similarity matrix: {item_sim_df.shape}\")\n"
      ]
    },
